cast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Steven Horsford (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Steven Horsford, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in Nevada's 4th District, a seat with a slight Democratic lean. He faces Republican Cody Whipple, a small-town rancher who has run the race his own way and raised about $1.2 million, though he enters the final weeks with under $80,000 on hand. Horsford has raised nearly $4 million and holds a cash advantage of more than $1 million, with little outside spending reported on either side.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on the district's lean, the money gap, and outside assessments. Ratings from ten outlets place the race at Likely Democratic or better, and prediction markets give Horsford roughly a 96 to 97 percent chance of winning. The district has flown under the radar compared with other Nevada House races, and recent coverage has centered on Horsford's legislative activity rather than a competitive contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 12.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9615, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9427, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9481, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9627, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9594, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9624, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 12.3}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9434, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9455, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.941, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9523, "mar